            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic 7-cm abdominal aortic aneurysm in an otherwise healthy 31-year-old woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>622-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1538574409335920</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal aortic aneurysms are rare in young women. We report the case of a 31-year-old woman who underwent open surgical repair of a symptomatic 7-cm abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA). The patient had no identifiable AAA risk factors. Laboratory and pathological analyses demonstrated a nonspecific inflammatory component.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
